## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: hif, Language: Fiji Hindi, Number of verses: 21
## References: Gambhir, S. K., & Moag, R. F. (1981). Fiji Hindi. A Basic Course and Reference Grammar. Journal of the American Oriental Society, 101(4), 506. https://doi.org/10.2307/601362 ; John, J. T., & Library, A. (2024). A dictionary of Urdu, classical Hindi, and English. Uchicago.edu. http://dsal.uchicago.edu/dictionaries/platts ; Shameem, N. (2002). Multilingual Proficiency in Fiji Primary Schools. Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development, 23(5), 388–407. https://doi.org/10.1080/01434630208666476 ; Shameem, N. (2017). Fiji Hindi in Fiji. In C. A. Seals & S. Shah (Eds.), Heritage Language Policies around the World. Routledge. ; Siegel, J. (1998). Indian languages in Fiji: Past, present and future. South Asia: Journal of South Asian Studies, 21, 181–214. https://doi.org/10.1080/00856409808723355

